<title>BRAZIL: GM Brazil to make Isuzu trucks.</title>
<headline>GM Brazil to make Isuzu trucks.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Corp's Brazilian affiliate will begin to manufacture Isuzu Motors trucks in Sao Paulo state in November, said a company official.</p>
<p>&quot;We will manufacture Isuzu trucks in Brazil with the GMC trademark as of November,&quot; said GM do Brasil truck division director Lellio Ramos.</p>
<p>Ramos said GM do Brasil plans to produce 2,500 Isuzu trucks annually. He said the company launched Isuzu trucks with the GMC trademark, imported from Japan, in July last year.</p>
<p>He also said Isuzu is fully integrated with General Motors as GM is Isuzu's largest single shareholder, with a 37 percent stake in the Japanese company.</p>
<p>((-- Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 2485412))</p>
